# Version 3 · the vow first, then why
title: Do Not Be Afraid
subtitle: Version 3 · The Vow
tempo: 84
key: E minor
music: solemn
intensity: 0.9
grade: dawn
images: ../assets/img/{}-2.webp
endnote: "Here I am! I stand at the door and knock."
endref: Revelation 3:20

@0:00-0:03 black cue:drone,0.4
audio: ../assets/audio/home-heart-1.mp3 gain 3db until 0:20 fade 0.5
@0:03-0:20 img:grown ken:in
text: I will not fear.
text: Fear makes the soul small.
text: Let it come.
text: Let it pass through me.
text: Only He remains.
@0:20-0:23 img:eyes ken:push hit:2
title: Why?
@0:23-0:25 drop:"The light shines in the darkness" ref:"John 1:5"
@0:25-0:31 img:child ken:up cue:wonder,0.8
vo: Because before anything was made, there was love.
@0:31-0:36 img:steps ken:down fx:flare
vo: Not a little. Not enough.
+2 title: Overflowing
@0:36-0:42 img:turn ken:in
vo: For the lost. For the misguided.
vo: Even for the ones who would wound Him.
@0:42-0:48 img:hands ken:slow fx:dove cue:wonder,1
vo: Nothing you do to the body can touch what He holds.
@0:48-0:54 img:kneel ken:in cue:tense,0.7
text: We love people.
text: We protect the little ones.
@0:54-1:00 img:millstone ken:down
vo: "Better for them to have a millstone hung around their neck..."
ref: Matthew 18:6
@1:00-1:06 img:door ken:push cue:tense,1
vo: "I never knew you."
ref: Matthew 7:23
@1:06-1:08 drop:"I am the way, the truth and the life" ref:"John 14:6"
@1:08-1:12 img:temple ken:right cue:build
text: Do not bargain with darkness.
@1:12-1:16 img:take ken:in
text: Drive it out.
@1:16-1:20.5 cuts:cords,knot,knot!,eyes,braid,whip cue:war
text: He made a whip of cords.
ref: John 2:15
@1:20.5-1:26 img:tables ken:slow hit:2
vo: "...and drove them all out of His Father's house."
@1:26-1:31 img:doves ken:up fx:flare cue:none
audio: ../assets/audio/home-choir-1.mp3 gain -2db until 1:35.8 fade 1.5
text: We do not fight people.
text: We fight for them.
@1:31-1:36 img:whipfloor ken:still
+1 title: Love is not weak.
@1:36-1:38 drop:"Take heart. I have overcome the world." ref:"John 16:33"
@1:38-1:45 img:weep ken:slow cue:weep
vo: He wept over the city that did not recognize the time of God's coming.
ref: Luke 19:41–44
@1:45-1:50 img:ruins ken:left hit:2
vo: "Not one stone will be left on another."
ref: Matthew 24:2 · 70 AD
@1:50-1:56 img:redsea ken:in cue:drone,0.8
sfx: braam
vo: "The Lord will fight for you. You need only to be still."
ref: Exodus 14:14
@1:56-2:00 img:eyesopen ken:still hold:silent
@2:00-2:07 img:stand ken:up fx:rise cue:tutti
vo: "Do not fear, for I am with you...
vo: I will uphold you with my righteous right hand."
ref: Isaiah 41:10
@2:07-2:10 img:dawn ken:push hit:2
audio: ../assets/audio/home-final-1.mp3 gain -3db
title: So stand.
@2:10-2:15 img:opendoor ken:in fade cue:outro
text: You were never forced.
text: You were invited.
@2:15-2:21 black
title: Do not be afraid.
